# ⚠⚠⚠ BUILD 190 — THE UN-IGNORE, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN TIDY.
#
# `ios/` above is UNANCHORED, so git matches it at EVERY depth — including
# `modules/tartaria-memory/ios/`, where this repository's only Tartaria-owned
# Swift lives. The first `git add modules/` staged the module's three JSON/TS
# files and SILENTLY DROPPED all four .swift files and the podspec. That would
# have pushed a local Expo module with no native source in it: autolinking finds
# expo-module.config.json, names `TartariaMemoryModule`, and the build dies on an
# EAS worker twenty minutes later with nothing in the diff to explain it.
#
# The rule above is correct and stays: `ios/` AT THE PROJECT ROOT is Expo CNG's
# generated prebuild output and must never be committed. This negation re-admits
# ONLY native source we author ourselves, under `modules/`.
#
# ⚠ THE DIRECTORY ITSELF HAS TO BE NEGATED, not the files inside it. Git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, so a `!modules/*/ios/**` written
# against the files alone is never consulted — the walk stops at the parent.
!modules/*/ios/

.tmp/
coverage/
.tartaria-tmp/

# Claude Code agent worktrees + local session scratch — never commit this.
.claude/
